# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession draft Blacksmithing --out` from Forever's client tables, trainer lists and data/forever. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/blacksmithing
title Blacksmithing 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Blacksmithing hammers bars into plate and mail, weapons, keys, rods, and the sharpening, weight
# and grinding stones the later recipes eat. Mining is its partner: every bar is smelted from ore,
# and the stones come straight from the veins. A Blacksmith Hammer must be in your bags, and almost
# every recipe needs an anvil (towns and forges have them).
#
# Forever's changes: almost every plan was moved 25 points down. It turns yellow, green and grey 25
# points sooner, and trainers teach it 25 points earlier (Runed Copper Belt from 45, Heavy Grinding
# Stone from 100), so a Classic route crafts grey recipes in about nine places. Copper Rod (for
# enchanters) is now Blacksmithing. Many new plans arrive in sets keyed to a gem or dust; most of
# them are sold for Merchant's Favor by Gor'mak near the Crossroads and Stondry Darkhammer at Three
# Corners (Redridge), and their later pieces need Sandpaper (Engineering) and Sulfuric Acid
# (Alchemy). Merchant's Favor is a currency from the supply crates turned in at the camps, not gold;
# its patterns bind when picked up. This route leaves them out.
#
# Camping: Sharpening Wheel (skill 20) is the Blacksmithing camp item. The Anvil (skill 140) is a
# camp station from a blueprint Gilnid drops in the Deadmines. The skill-300 Master Forge has no
# known blueprint source, and about 60 late plans need it.
#
# Ranks: Journeyman needs character level 10 (Forever's sniffed lists). Trainers teach by tier and
# train only from their tier's skill: Journeyman at the city trainers, from skill 50; Expert only at
# Bengus Deepforge (Ironforge) and Saru Steelfury (Orgrimmar), from 125; Artisan only at Brikk
# Keencraft (Booty Bay), from 200. Specialisation at 200 and level 40: Armorsmith (Grumnus
# Steelshaper, Ironforge / Okothos Ironrager, Orgrimmar) or Weaponsmith (Ironus Coldsteel, Ironforge
# / Borgosh Corebender, Orgrimmar), with the axe, hammer and sword masters in Everlook at 250 and
# level 50.
#
# Route (crafts are expected counts; yellow and green crafts can take more):
#     1-35  Rough Sharpening Stone, about 42 (known): 1 Rough Stone each
#    35-75  Rough Grinding Stone, about 64 (trainer 1s): 2 Rough Stone each
#    75-100 Runed Copper Belt, about 29 (trainer 2s): 10 Copper Bar each
#   100-125 Patterned Bronze Bracers, about 25 (trainer 5s): 5 Bronze Bar and 2 Coarse Grinding Stone each
#   125-150 Bronze Warhammer, about 25 (trainer 2s 50c): 8 Bronze Bar, 1 Strong Flux and 1 Medium Leather each
#   150-175 Green Iron Bracers, about 28 (trainer): 6 Iron Bar and 1 Green Dye each
#   175-185 Golden Scale Bracers, about 10 (trainer): 5 Steel Bar and 2 Heavy Grinding Stone each
#   185-200 Heavy Mithril Gauntlet, about 15 (trainer): 6 Mithril Bar and 4 Mageweave Cloth each
#   200-215 Steel Plate Helm, about 16 (trainer): 14 Steel Bar and 1 Solid Grinding Stone each
#   215-225 Heavy Mithril Boots, about 10 (trainer): 14 Mithril Bar and 4 Thick Leather each
#   225-235 Dense Weightstone, about 17 (trainer): 1 Dense Stone each
#   235-240 Heavy Mithril Boots, about 8 (trainer): 14 Mithril Bar and 4 Thick Leather each
#   240-245 Imperial Plate Belt, about 5 (quest, 20 Thorium Bar): 22 Thorium Bar, 6 Rugged Leather and 1 Aquamarine each
#   245-265 Imperial Plate Bracers, about 20 (quest, 20 Thorium Bar): 20 Thorium Bar and 1 Star Ruby each
#   265-291 Radiant Boots, about 27 (pattern from the Auction House): 14 Thorium Bar and 4 Heart of Fire each
#   291-300 Radiant Leggings, about 9 (pattern from the Auction House): 20 Thorium Bar and 4 Heart of Fire each
#   with Derotain's plans:
#     265-270 Imperial Plate Bracers, about 6 (quest, 20 Thorium Bar): 20 Thorium Bar and 1 Star Ruby each
#     270-300 Imperial Plate Boots, about 34 (quest, 40 Thorium Bar): 34 Thorium Bar, 1 Star Ruby and 1 Aquamarine each
#
# Shopping per bracket (vendor goods at vendor prices; gathered or dropped materials by count, enough for 9 players in 10):
# 1-75: Apprentice 10c, recipes 1s; gather or buy 195 Rough Stone.
# 75-150: Journeyman 5s, recipes 12s, vendor goods 5g 18c; gather or buy 25 Medium Leather, 100
# Coarse Stone, 320 Copper Bar and 325 Bronze Bar.
# 150-225: Expert 50s (Classic price), recipes 10s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 28s;
# gather or buy 60 Heavy Stone, 186 Iron Bar, 302 Steel Bar, 230 Mithril Bar, 84 Thick Leather, 60
# Mageweave Cloth and 72 Solid Stone.
# 225-300: Artisan 5g (Classic price), trainer recipes (prices not in the data); gather or buy 154
# Mithril Bar, 5 Aquamarine, 20 Star Ruby, 30 Rugged Leather, 550 Thorium Bar and 24 Dense Stone.
# 265-300 (with Radiant plans): nothing to buy; gather or buy 152 Heart of Fire and 586 Thorium Bar.
# 265-300 (with Derotain's plans): nothing to buy; gather or buy 37 Aquamarine, 45 Star Ruby and
# 1458 Thorium Bar.
#
# Data: recipes, colours and reagents from the Forever client's tables; trainer learn skills and
# prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists (they reach skill 50-150); vendors, stock and drops
# from data/forever. Materials are valued at about four times their vendor sell price (cloth and
# leather by the square root of it, hides four times higher; tools/lib/professions/materials.js) to
# rank recipes against each other, never as a price forecast.
# Learn skills players' recordings bear out (estimated from Classic's lists; the lowest skill
# players learned each at, never below): Green Iron Bracers 140 (19 players), Solid Grinding Stone
# 175 (8 players) and Dense Weightstone 225 (4 players).
# ASSUMED: learn skills of Golden Scale Bracers 160, Heavy Mithril Gauntlet 180, Steel Plate Helm
# 190 and Heavy Mithril Boots 210 (no sniffed Forever list teaches them: Classic's trainer skill
# moved as far as Forever moved the recipe's colours, which the sniffed lists bear out on 126 of 129
# recipes). In-game check: the skill the trainer asks; their prices are not in the data.
# ASSUMED: rank level gates Expert 20 and Artisan 35 (Classic's; Forever's sniffed lists ask level 1
# for Apprentice and 10 for Journeyman). In-game check: the level each trainer asks.
# ASSUMED: Derotain Mudsipper's Imperial Plate quests ask Blacksmithing 240 and character level 50
# (a recorded blacksmith of 243 was offered all of them, where the quest data still has Classic's
# 265; 240 is where his first plans, the belt's, can be learned). In-game check: the skill his
# quests ask.
# ASSUMED: rank prices Expert 50s and Artisan 5g (Classic's trainer lists; Forever's sniffed lists
# price only Apprentice 10c and Journeyman 5s, as in Classic). In-game check: what Expert and
# Artisan cost.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice (1-75)
section Blacksmithing 1-75

step Learn Blacksmithing
  tip Apprentice Blacksmithing lets you craft up to 75 for 10c, at any character level. Any Blacksmithing trainer of your faction teaches it; the arrow picks the nearest. Buy a Blacksmith Hammer (any blacksmithing supplier) and pair it with Mining: Rough Stone and Copper Ore come from the Copper Veins of every starting zone. 1-75 takes about 1s of recipes, plus 195 Rough Stone to gather or buy.
  train Blacksmithing Apprentice
  skill Blacksmithing 1

step Get Rough Stone
  tip 195 Rough Stone for Blacksmithing 1-75: 47 Rough Sharpening Stones and 74 Rough Grinding Stones. Mining: Copper Vein (skill 1) in Dun Morogh (1-10), Elwynn Forest (1-10) and Zephras Isle (1-15). The arrow takes the Mining loop that gets you them soonest from where you are and walks it until your bags hold them; the window names the loop, its lap and the laps left. Or buy them at the Auction House.
