step Green Iron Bracers to 175
  tip Green Iron Bracers is orange at 150 (yellow 165, green 177, grey 190): about 28 crafts to 175, up to 31 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 6 Iron Bar and 1 Green Dye. Six Iron Bars and a Green Dye a craft; Green Dye comes from tailoring, leatherworking and trade supplies vendors. Orange to 165 on Forever, so a point every craft for the first fifteen. Needs an anvil nearby.
  craft 3501 until 175

step Blacksmithing recipes at 175
  tip Back to Bengus Deepforge (Ironforge) (Alliance) or Saru Steelfury (Orgrimmar) (Horde): Golden Scale Bracers (from 160) and Solid Grinding Stone (from 175).
  learn 7223 npc 4258 only Alliance
  learn 7223 npc 3355 only Horde
  learn 9920 npc 4258 only Alliance
  learn 9920 npc 3355 only Horde

step Golden Scale Bracers to 185
  tip Golden Scale Bracers is orange at 175 (yellow 185, green 197, grey 210): about 10 crafts to 185, a point every craft. Each takes 5 Steel Bar and 2 Heavy Grinding Stone. Make the 20 Heavy Grinding Stone first. Steel Bars are smelted from an Iron Bar and a Coal (Mining 165; Coal from trade and blacksmithing suppliers), so each bracer is five of each. Each bracer takes two Heavy Grinding Stones: make them first. Needs an anvil nearby.
  craft 3337 x20
  craft 7223 until 185

step Blacksmithing recipes at 185
  tip Back to Bengus Deepforge (Ironforge) (Alliance) or Saru Steelfury (Orgrimmar) (Horde): Heavy Mithril Gauntlet (from 180).
  learn 9928 npc 4258 only Alliance
  learn 9928 npc 3355 only Horde

step Heavy Mithril Gauntlet to 200
  tip Heavy Mithril Gauntlet is orange at 185 (yellow 200, green 210, grey 220): about 15 crafts to 200, a point every craft. Each takes 6 Mithril Bar and 4 Mageweave Cloth. Six Mithril Bars and four Mageweave Cloth a craft; Bengus Deepforge (Ironforge) and Saru Steelfury (Orgrimmar) teach it from 180. Needs an anvil nearby.
  craft 9928 until 200

step Blacksmithing recipes at 200
  tip Back to Bengus Deepforge (Ironforge) (Alliance) or Saru Steelfury (Orgrimmar) (Horde): Steel Plate Helm (from 190).
  learn 9935 npc 4258 only Alliance
  learn 9935 npc 3355 only Horde

step Steel Plate Helm to 215
  tip Steel Plate Helm is orange at 200 (yellow 210, green 220, grey 230): about 16 crafts to 215, up to 18 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 14 Steel Bar and 1 Solid Grinding Stone. Make the 16 Solid Grinding Stone first. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data. Specialisation (optional): at 200 and character level 40, Grumnus Steelshaper (Ironforge) or Okothos Ironrager (Orgrimmar) starts The Art of the Armorsmith: 4 Ornate Mithril Helms, 2 Ornate Mithril Boots and an Ornate Mithril Breastplate, whose plans come from a Mithril Order quest chain. Ironus Coldsteel (Ironforge) or Borgosh Corebender (Orgrimmar) starts The Way of the Weaponsmith: 4 Moonsteel Broadswords, 4 Massive Iron Axes, 2 Heavy Mithril Axes and 2 Big Black Maces; on Forever the Moonsteel Broadsword plans (Zarena Cromwind, Booty Bay) and Massive Iron Axe plans bind when picked up, so buy and use them yourself. You can take only one; neither is needed for 300, and the beta never tested them (it stopped at level 30). Needs an anvil nearby.
  craft 9920 x16
  craft 9935 until 215

step Blacksmithing recipes at 215
  tip Heavy Mithril Boots (from 210) is taught only by the Artisan trainers: Alliance Brikk Keencraft (Stranglethorn Vale); Horde Brikk Keencraft (Stranglethorn Vale). You can train Artisan there now if you are level 35 (it needs Blacksmithing 200), which saves the trip at 225.
  learn 9968 npc 2836 only Alliance
  learn 9968 npc 2836 only Horde
  train Blacksmithing Artisan optional

step Heavy Mithril Boots to 225
  tip Heavy Mithril Boots is orange at 215 (yellow 230, green 240, grey 250): about 10 crafts to 225, a point every craft. Each takes 14 Mithril Bar and 4 Thick Leather. Mithril Bars from Mithril Deposits; Thick Leather from skinners or the Auction House. Needs an anvil nearby. Blacksmithing 225 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 9968 until 225
  skill Blacksmithing 225

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Artisan (225-300)
section Blacksmithing 225-300

step Artisan Blacksmithing
  tip Artisan raises the cap from 225 to 300 for 5g (Classic's price; Forever's is not in the data); it needs Blacksmithing 200 and character level 35, so you can take it on any visit from 200. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Brikk Keencraft (Stranglethorn Vale); Horde Brikk Keencraft (Stranglethorn Vale). This route trains it at Brikk Keencraft (Stranglethorn Vale) for the Alliance and Brikk Keencraft (Stranglethorn Vale) for the Horde, who also teach the recipes of 225-300: one trainer for every visit. Learn now: Dense Weightstone (from 225). 225-300 takes 154 Mithril Bar, 5 Aquamarine, 20 Star Ruby, 30 Rugged Leather, 550 Thorium Bar and 24 Dense Stone to gather or buy. From 265 the route splits: with Radiant plans, about 36 more crafts and 152 Heart of Fire and 586 Thorium Bar; with Derotain's plans, about 40 crafts and 37 Aquamarine, 45 Star Ruby and 1458 Thorium Bar.
  level 35
  train Blacksmithing Artisan npc 2836 only Alliance
  train Blacksmithing Artisan npc 2836 only Horde
  learn 16640 npc 2836 only Alliance
  learn 16640 npc 2836 only Horde

